\name{BaseRDirectedGraphLayerProcessor}
\alias{BaseRDirectedGraphLayerProcessor}
\title{Base R Directed Graph Layer Processor}
\description{
Reads \code{plot()} of a directed igraph object -- igraph's own \code{plot.igraph()}
-- as a directed graph: one node per vertex, in vertex order, each naming
the vertices whose edges arrive at it, with its own attributes, read from
the graph rather than the drawing. Each node is outlined as its own
circle: \code{plot.igraph()} draws every circle vertex with one \code{symbols()}
call, in vertex order, and gridGraphics exports that call as one group of
\verb{<circle>} elements.

Emitted with \code{type = "directed_graph"}, which the core has read since
maidr 4.14.0.
}
\keyword{internal}
